{"name":"Chicon","hex":"#d9eeb4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Chicon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A name given to various science fiction conventions held in Chicago, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Chicon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Belgian endive","blocks":[{"text":"Belgian endive, also known as witloof chicory or chicon, is a lettuce-like vegetable or salad green. Belgian endive was developed in Belgium in the 1850s and is nicknamed \"white gold\" in that country. In 2021 Brussels added it to the region's Inventory of Intangible Cultural Heritage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Endive_p1160063.jpg/330px-Endive_p1160063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgian_endive"},{"title":"Chicon (Worldcon)","blocks":[{"text":"Chicon is the name given to seven Worldcons and retroactively applied to an eighth Worldcon. All eight of the conventions were held in Chicago, Illinois."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicon_(Worldcon)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Chicory_%28witlof%29%2C_oven_dish_with_ham_and_cheese.jpg/500px-Chicory_%28witlof%29%2C_oven_dish_with_ham_and_cheese.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Chicory_%28witlof%29%2C_oven_dish_with_ham_and_cheese.jpg/1280px-Chicory_%28witlof%29%2C_oven_dish_with_ham_and_cheese.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Chicory_%28witlof%29%2C_oven_dish_with_ham_and_cheese.jpg/500px-Chicory_%28witlof%29%2C_oven_dish_with_ham_and_cheese.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Endive au jambon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChicory_(wi